===Etymology===
{{named-after|en|{{w|Caspar Friedrich Wolff}}|nat=German|occ=physiologist|born=1733|died=1794}}, who described the [[mesonephros]] and its ducts in his dissertation in 1759.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|embryology}} A [[paired]] [[structure]] found in [[mammal]]s including humans that [[develop]]s in the early stages of [[embryonic]] [[development]] and plays a [[critical]] role in the [[formation]] of [[male]] [[reproductive organ]]s.
#: {{syn|en|mesonephric duct}}
#: {{cot|en|Müllerian duct}}

